# Daemon-Core

Daemon-Core is a modular Linux desktop shell framework built around Wayland, Hyprland, Quickshell, Qt 6, and greetd. It is designed as a unified shell platform for login, lockscreen, bar, dashboard, notifications, control center, and theming.

## Goals

- Unified desktop shell experience
- Theme-driven design
- Service-based architecture
- Modular feature development
- Clear configuration and state management
- Safe fallback behavior

## Project status

This repository is currently in the architecture and planning phase, with the foundation for modules, themes, and services being defined and stabilized.

## Architecture summary

```text
System / Wayland / Hyprland
        ↓
IPC adapters
        ↓
Services
        ↓
Shared components
        ↓
Feature modules
        ↓
User interface
```

